<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Downstream utility.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2" title="Downstream utility. ‣ 5.3 Additional Analyses ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ MUSE: Agentic 3D Scene Authoring via Memory-Grounded Incremental Requirement Satisfaction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a> evaluates 100 three-stage navigation curricula, producing 300 scenes per method. While both incremental MUSE and stage-wise regeneration produce navigable final scenes (high reachable ratios, zero collisions), MUSE yields substantially stronger spatial continuity. It achieves higher difficulty monotonicity (0.850 vs. 0.394) and free-space preservation (0.978 vs. 0.649). This confirms that incremental authoring provides not merely static navigability, but a stable, predictable spatial substrate useful for navigation-oriented embodied-AI settings.</p>
</div>
